to","reason":"''Have'' (possession) is a state, so would is not possible."},{"id":"CP1-06","week":2,"target":"Main: intention","prompt":"A: Any plans for the summer? B: I ___ visit my cousins in Ireland, but I haven''t booked anything yet.","options":["''m going to","''m visiting"],"key":"''m going to","reason":"An intention with nothing arranged yet."},{"id":"CP1-07","week":2,"target":"Main: arrangement","prompt":"We ___ (fly) to Lisbon on Friday. The tickets are in my bag.","options":[],"key":"''re flying (are flying)","reason":"A fixed arrangement."},{"id":"CP1-08","week":2,"target":"Main: time clause","prompt":"I''ll send you the photos when I ___ home.","options":["get","''ll get"],"key":"get","reason":"After ''when'', use the present simple for the future."},{"id":"CP1-09","week":2,"target":"Main: time clause","prompt":"As soon as the film ___ (finish), we''ll go for dinner.","options":[],"key":"finishes","reason":"After ''as soon as'', use the present simple for the future."},{"id":"CP1-10","week":2,"target":"Light","prompt":"If I ___ the lottery, I''d buy a house by the sea.","options":["won","win"],"key":"won","reason":"Second conditional: an imagined situation."},{"id":"CP1-11","week":3,"target":"Main: obligation","prompt":"In the UK, you ___ drive on the left.","options":["have to","don''t have to"],"key":"have to","reason":"It is a rule."},{"id":"CP1-12","week":3,"target":"Main: advice","prompt":"If you want to improve your English, you ___ read a little every day.","options":["should","mustn''t"],"key":"should","reason":"Advice."},{"id":"CP1-13","week":3,"target":"Main: ability","prompt":"My grandmother ___ (can / not / use) a smartphone, so we phone her.","options":[],"key":"can''t use (cannot use)","reason":"Ability, negative."},{"id":"CP1-14","week":3,"target":"Main: permission","prompt":"___ I leave my bag here while I go to the toilet?","options":["Can","Must"],"key":"Can (Could)","reason":"Asking for permission."},{"id":"CP1-15","week":3,"target":"Light","prompt":"Put the words in order: Where / you / do / work?","options":[],"key":"Where do you work?","reason":"Auxiliary before the subject."},{"id":"CP1-16","week":4,"target":"Main: present passive","prompt":"Cheese ___ (make) from milk.","options":[],"key":"is made","reason":"A general fact; the cheese is the focus."},{"id":"CP1-17","week":4,"target":"Main: present passive","prompt":"Most of the city''s buses ___ by electricity now.","options":["are powered","power"],"key":"are powered","reason":"Something powers the buses."},{"id":"CP1-18","week":4,"target":"Main: past passive","prompt":"The first email ___ (send) in 1971.","options":[],"key":"was sent","reason":"Past passive."},{"id":"CP1-19","week":4,"target":"Main: past passive","prompt":"Our flight ___ because of the snow.","options":["was cancelled","cancelled"],"key":"was cancelled","reason":"The airline cancelled it."},{"id":"CP1-20","week":4,"target":"Light","prompt":"This is the hotel ___ we stayed last summer.","options":["where","who"],"key":"where","reason":"''Where'' for a place followed by a full clause."}],"reserves":[{"id":"CP1-R1","week":1,"target":"reserve","prompt":"I ___ (not / see) her since the wedding.","options":[],"key":"haven''t seen (have not seen)","reason":"Up to now with since."},{"id":"CP1-R2","week":2,"target":"reserve","prompt":"Don''t worry, I ___ (call) you before I ___ (leave).","options":[],"key":"''ll call ... leave","reason":"Will for the promise; present simple after before."},{"id":"CP1-R3","week":3,"target":"reserve","prompt":"You ___ (not / have to) come to the party if you''re tired.","options":[],"key":"don''t have to","reason":"It isn''t necessary."},{"id":"CP1-R4","week":4,"target":"reserve","prompt":"The Alhambra ___ (visit) by millions of people every year.","options":[],"key":"is visited","reason":"Present passive with by."}],"reserveUse":"Reserves replace an item that pilot data shows is unclear, or form a retake for learners repeating the checkpoint.","writing":{"prompts":[{"label":"A. A change I got used to","text":"Describe how life was before a change, what happened, what was difficult, and how things are now."},{"label":"B. A note for a visitor","text":"A friend is visiting your town for a weekend. Recommend what to see: include a regular event or custom, one fact about a place''s past, a comparison, and one piece of advice."}],"conditions":[{"id":"length","setting":"Length","value":"150 words (130–170 accepted)"},{"id":"time","setting":"Time","value":"30 minutes, with a visible timer"},{"id":"where","setting":"Where","value":"In the app; pasting disabled; no phrase bank or model"},{"id":"attempts","setting":"Attempts","value":"One submission; no revise-and-retry"},{"id":"marking","setting":"Marking","value":"AI bands on the four writing criteria straight away; a teacher confirms where one is involved, and the teacher''s mark counts"}],"onTarget":"''On target'' or better on at least three criteria, task achievement not ''Getting there''. Results guide practice; they never block week 5."},"result":{"intro":"Results are reported by part and by week, never as pass or fail. Learners continue to week 5 whatever their result; the checkpoint guides practice, it does not block progress.","thresholds":[{"part":"Quiz","onTarget":"14 of 20 or more (70%)"},{"part":"Speaking","onTarget":"''On target'' or better on at least three criteria, and task achievement not at ''Getting there''"},{"part":"Writing","onTarget":"''On target'' or better on at least three criteria, and task achievement not at ''Getting there''"}],"practiceLinks":"Each part below target links to the matching practice: weak quiz items to that week''s extra items and grammar clinic, speaking to the week''s shadowing and conversation, writing to a revise-and-retry task on the same prompt."},"calibration":["A second teacher checks every checkpoint item for a single correct answer and accepted variants.","Check the existing 24 placement questions against the blueprint (6 A2, 8 B1, 6 B1+, 4 B2) and replace those that do not fit.","Mark 10–20 sample texts and recordings by hand and compare with the AI''s bands; adjust prompts until they agree on at least 8 in 10.","After 30 placed learners, compare placement with EF SET results and adjust the cut scores (11/12 and 18/19).","Review any checkpoint item that more than 90% or fewer than 30% of pilot learners answer correctly.","Confirm the checkpoint thresholds (70% quiz, three of four criteria) against teacher judgement of pilot learners."],"speaking":{"status":"pilot draft — pending second-teacher review","intro":"After week 4, learners record one short spoken narrative under checkpoint conditions, marked with the same four descriptors.","prompt":"Talk about a time when you had to adapt to something new: a job, a place, a course or a routine. What was it like before, what happened, and how are things now? If you like, say what you would tell someone in the same situation.","conditions":[{"setting":"Planning","value":"1 minute; notes allowed, no phrase bank or model"},{"setting":"Length","value":"60-90 seconds"},{"setting":"Attempts","value":"One recording; no retry (practice tasks allow retries, checkpoints do not)"},{"setting":"Marking","value":"AI bands on the four criteria straight away; a teacher confirms where one is involved, and the teacher''s mark counts"},{"setting":"On target","value":"\"On target\" or better on at least three of the four criteria, with no criterion at \"Getting there\" for task achievement"},{"setting":"Language it draws on","value":"Weeks 1-4: narrative tenses, present perfect, used to / would, modals for advice; featured vocabulary from any of the four weeks"}],"transferNote":"The prompt is new, so it tests transfer rather than memory of a practised answer."}},"status":"pilot draft — pending second-teacher review","sources":["Writing descriptors, placement and checkpoint 1 (21 Nov 2026)","Fluency Studio: Weeks 1–4 Speaking Content (21 Nov 2026)"]}'::jsonb->'checkpoint1')
on conflict (code) do update set title = excluded.title, payload = excluded.payload;

